-- Phase 2b of the NPC / bestiary work, second half: every named being Rifts
-- Conversion Book Two: Pantheons of the Megaverse stats - the Aztec, Babylonian,
-- Greek, Hindu, Norse and Persian pantheons, their Rifts Earth impostors and
-- champions, and their named mounts and monsters - rows for notable_npcs
-- (migration 072) and their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
-- FOUND by the filing rule of migration 072: a stat block with a Real Name or
-- Greek Name line, or a numeric experience level. Race and R.C.C. templates
-- (Godlings, Nagas, Valkyries, Galla...), unnamed minion types and the blank
-- character sheet at the back are not rows.
--
-- NAMES. This book prints impostors and champions under a god's own name: Zeus
-- the Thunderer is Trellacryth, Hercules of Olympus is Herbert Rowland, the Dark
-- Council's Enlil is Krellon. The true god keeps the plain slug; each other one
-- takes its heading's epithet (zeus-the-thunderer). Dragons and Gods has its own
-- Hel, so this book's is hel-norse.
--
-- EXTRACTED by thirteen book-extract-workers, every number read off a 200 dpi
-- render rather than the OCR cache - the text layer carries the digit cipher and
-- drops whole lines (Zurvan's attributes) - and every printed folio checked
-- against scripts/books.json. RECONCILED by book-reconcile against the renders,
-- row by row; its corrections are applied.
--
-- WHAT A ROW HOLDS. The book's numbers, as printed; an attribute the book does not
-- print is absent, never invented. Where two values are printed (Rifts Earth
-- M.D.C., a god's apparent and true strength) the first is in the field and the
-- other in bonuses_note. description, disposition and natural_abilities are short
-- paraphrases - no sentence is the book's.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-notable-npcs-pantheons.sql
--
-- BY BOOK:
